message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Wetland Water Mapping with Random Forest"
abstract: "Google Earth Engine script that maps open water in lakes and wetlands from Landsat 5/7/8/9 with a Random Forest trained on eight spectral water indices. It reports a spatially blocked hold-out check, variable importance, area-adjusted map accuracy and area estimates with 95% confidence intervals from a stratified random sample (Olofsson et al., 2014), quantity and allocation disagreement (Pontius and Millones, 2011), and a multi-decade water-area time series with the observed area and cloud percentage of each year."
type: software
